  "response_text": "The __io_putchar function defines how the standard printf function outputs characters to a hardware interface, commonly UART. While printf is part of the C standard library, it lacks direct hardware support. By implementing __io_putchar, character output can be routed to specific peripherals. In this lab, the function enabled communication with a serial terminal via UART. Modifying this function allows redirection of output to other devices, such as USB or an LCD, making it an essential component in adapting standard output functions for embedded environments.\\n",
